{"title":"2016 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Use_One_Variable)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Use One Variable)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Formal)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Formal)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5:_Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5: Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Alice and Bob live <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles apart. One day Alice looks due north from her house and sees an airplane. At the same time Bob looks due west from his house and sees the same airplane. The angle of elevation of the airplane is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> from Alice's position and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29fa0a9949f018e121b2093216dd5db13d3abef0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> from Bob's position. Which of the following is closest to the airplane's altitude, in miles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/4/da490a7c86a0c2a3c842a424e0bfb069e9600b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4.5 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"391\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's set the altitude = z, distance from Alice to airplane's ground position (point right below airplane)=y and distance from Bob to airplane's ground position=x\n</p><p>From Alice's point of view, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1942e1c2e3bf402a1ec7fd4e128d02be39f150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta)=\\frac{z}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"85\" height=\"36\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/0/2c05d0dd5148e5725cf0ef3b72aefb6c98b159b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{30}=\\frac{\\sin{30}}{\\cos{30}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"172\" height=\"42\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b9dece3d43ae9440306c054950c7280314edab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=z*\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>From Bob's point of view, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/4/c14b95b538c175bfc4b522e3d06195560594a8b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(\\theta)=\\frac{z}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"86\" height=\"33\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/6198e03577c63d5c453f2294a1ec346427174ba8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan{60}=\\frac{\\sin{60}}{\\cos{60}}=\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"170\" height=\"37\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d94fe99330887954d53c66e1fb7e0c292ba324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{z}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"61\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> + <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/a/f5a3faa3658bcbd8bde8e16cfa5baf019619fc9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db61fd75a1a8bb6fa2b202b6b73daf9b4c9838d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Solving the equation (by plugging in x and y), we get z=<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/d/7edef3e943c3e7f25309279e268b0b120036bbbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" /> = about 5.5.  \n</p><p>So, answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c89b39a1621ea0c8b65f454443cec3dab6730a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E) 5.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"47\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>solution by sudeepnarala\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Use_One_Variable.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Use_One_Variable)\">Solution 2 (Use One Variable)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Use One Variable)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have two 30-60-90 triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00cb04571fd7efc09d2de1b2da589ee6a5b7756d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DBC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> that are perpendicular and share leg <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> (the altitude of the plane <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/f/7ffcdfbb239f4fc6927d010456a569ad5d1ef307.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" /> The shared leg is the shortest leg of one triangle and the longest leg of the other. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are Bob and Alice respectively.\n</p><p><br />\nFind <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27e525b776c49bbe7d0ae66cfc7ab8f58f40624e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Use Pythagorean Theorem on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840cb55c82434b9ae047760636a017e9441e6ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> to produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/b/6db170e22e0bbd11770a24e09d786562b2d9a972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=\\sqrt{30}\\implies\\boxed{\\textbf{E)}\\ 5.5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"177\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<pre><b>EXAMPLE</b>: Let angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be 30 degrees and angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be 60 degrees. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77ba556a75177e008085f0f10e3d2475addc13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=p\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/6/0362000e06dc269f4f46297e15d661c72c231d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=\\frac{p}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" /> by special triangle rules. By Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/6/a26e650ceb77091a1fbca76278cae6f1fe201a0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC^2+DC^2=AB^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c07f03b99b464db1bab69871f5ec5ccaec4b63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(p\\sqrt{3})^2+(\\frac{p}{\\sqrt{3}})^2=10^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"175\" height=\"37\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/4/b8405cd9fb796e7bb6e187884a75b6fdb8df3111.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=\\sqrt{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />\n</pre>\n<p>(Solution by BJHHar)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Non-trig solution by e_power_pi_times_i\n</p><p><br />\nSet the distance from Alice's and Bob's position to the point directly below the airplane to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, respectively. From the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb34185cd64050955935222d90913c9938606130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />. As both are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangles, the altitude of the airplane can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/7/887d30fa8b6f6d9faf5e89158866759b0c4c246e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x\\sqrt{3}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"37\" height=\"41\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/9/5b906ed8e9a3049e5435cd88ee75e16109a09887.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" />. Solving the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/08180213830f6d6decdac4e2d639e851141f20c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{x\\sqrt{3}}{3} = y\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"97\" height=\"41\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c6b57636c75f12e872cde8c6fab9d64d9151a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 3y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />. Plugging this into the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb34185cd64050955935222d90913c9938606130.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"18\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c9c7eb373e38017a11f79b122fedbffeae4c188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10y^2 = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c132844cdc1b0661b507259ade46b0fdd9d706c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\sqrt{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"20\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> cannot be negative), so the altitude is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/6/5c624cfc9091e7e5bf297c6c046161962cee5762.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3*10} = \\sqrt{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />, which is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f81f588ba1da2107ed6537c9f733335dfdd018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{E)}\\ 5.5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"60\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Formal.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Formal)\">Solution 4 (Formal)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Formal)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Alice be at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, Bob be at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. Let the plane be at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the projection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto the ground (the plane with contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />). Let the height of the plane, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fc2c59d25e97ec515446444b44cbe415d3f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" />, be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. So, because of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> triangles,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d17ccf85e925fba03cbe2e3c456884fc8d7192f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AX = \\dfrac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}, BX = h\\sqrt{3}\\]\" width=\"181\" height=\"42\" />\nBy <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82e88b3efdcfe5340faa5a70a547e07bbaf9d87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABX$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/e/83e80271d692e207bf60777e808d423dc95d2fa6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{h^2}{3} + 3h^2 = 100 \\implies \\dfrac{10h^2}{3} = 100 \\implies h = \\sqrt{30},\\]\" width=\"383\" height=\"39\" />\nwhich is clossest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/5/ed517bcb7a7b85091e9370b76e7180e29fd64df1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 5.5}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"74\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~sml1809\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5:_Diagram\">Solution 5: Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93d76df907d3a2a62096b20a1d8b02ab90e7ba56.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; size(8cm); currentprojection = perspective(camera=(3,-3,1), up=Z);  real h = sqrt(30); real AX = h * sqrt(3); real BX = h / sqrt(3);  triple X = (0,0,0); triple A = (0,-AX,0); triple B = (BX,0,0); triple P = (0,0,h);  // Triangle at gruond draw(A--X--B--cycle);  // Vertical and slant edges draw(X--P, dashed); draw(A--P); draw(B--P);  // Right angles real s = 0.6; // size of right angle marks path3 angle_AXB = X -- X+(s,0,0) -- X+(s,-s,0) -- X+(0,-s,0) -- cycle; path3 angle_PXA = X -- X+(0,-s,0) -- X+(0,-s,s) -- X+(0,0,s) -- cycle; path3 angle_PXB = X -- X+(s,0,0) -- X+(s,0,s) -- X+(0,0,s) -- cycle;  draw(angle_AXB); draw(angle_PXA); draw(angle_PXB);  // Mark angle of elevation from Alice real arc_radius = 1.0; triple vAX = unit(X-A); triple vAP = unit(P-A); triple normalA = cross(vAX, vAP); path3 arc30 = arc(A, A + arc_radius*vAX, A + arc_radius*vAP, normalA); draw(arc30); triple bisectorA = unit(vAX + vAP); label(&quot;$30^\\circ$&quot;, A + (arc_radius + 0.9)*bisectorA);  // Mark angle of elevation from Bob (60°) triple vBX = unit(X-B); triple vBP = unit(P-B); triple normalB = cross(vBX, vBP); path3 arc60 = arc(B, B + arc_radius*vBX, B + arc_radius*vBP, normalB); draw(arc60); triple bisectorB = unit(vBX + vBP); label(&quot;$60^\\circ$&quot;, B + (arc_radius + 0.6)*bisectorB);  // Label points label(&quot;Alice&quot;, A, SW); label(&quot;Bob&quot;, B, SE); label(&quot;Plane&quot;, P, N); label(&quot;$X$&quot;, X + (0,-0.4,0.4), NW);  // Distance between Alice and Bob label(&quot;$10$&quot;, midpoint(A--B), S);  dot(A); dot(B); dot(X); dot(P); [/asy]\" width=\"368\" height=\"232\" />\n</p><p>~credit to mathmaster2012 for original diagram\n</p><p>~BakedPotato66 added/contributed some elements\n</p><p>~Blosp Refactored diagram\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_.28Problem_11-20.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CanadaMath_(Problem_11-20)\">Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CanadaMath (Problem 11-20)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fast Forward to 9:16 for problem 13\n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4osvFatUv1o</a>\n</p><p>~THEMATHCANADIAN\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B\">2016 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" a